  "details": "Eac mismatch error. \n\n1. Open vrchat, \n\n2 receive error  eac vrchat mismatch/verify files \n\n3. Go into steam vrchat settings , verify files\n\n4. Changes nothing keeps happening consistently every other time I launch vrchat.\n\nAdditionally: \n\n5. Go into steam deck desktop mode \n\n6. Find vrchat in local steam app folder\n\n7. Delete files related to vrchat and uninstall vrchat on steam \n\n8 reinstall. \n\n9. Error persists as usual. \n\n2nd error crashing (more recent issue )\n\n1. Try to load into game\n\n2. Play for a bit crash alot.\n\n3. Eventually it gets bad enough to not get able to load into game at all \n\n4.repeat steps 5 through 8 in previous error \n\n5. Load vrchat it lets me in\n\n6. Only within a few hours or so go back to step one of this error. And rinse repeat.",
